WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:31.541
In the previous two verses,

2
00:00:31.541 --> 00:00:33.333
Lord Krishna gave us deep,

3
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.125
secret knowledge.

4
00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:37.458
But He knew that we might struggle

5
00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:39.541
to fully grasp it,

6
00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:42.083
and that contradictions might
 arise in our minds.

7
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.625
So in this verse, He explains
 that same knowledge

8
00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:47.458
through a beautiful analogy.

9
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.791
How does Lord Krishna remain unattached

10
00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:56.666
even while being

11
00:00:56.666 --> 00:00:59.541
the master of all creation?

12
00:00:59.541 --> 00:01:01.000
This question may well be arising

13
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.791
in your mind.

14
00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:05.625
And do you know why?

15
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:08.000
Because we as humans

16
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.750
are unfamiliar with Lord Krishna’s divine powers.

17
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.916
We try to understand everything

18
00:01:13.916 --> 00:01:15.958
through logic alone.

19
00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:18.541
So through this verse,

20
00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:20.875
Lord Krishna wants us to understand –

21
00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:23.833
He is like the sky, and all living beings

22
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:25.250
are like the wind

23
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.500
that moves through it.

24
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.958
Just as the wind moves freely through the sky

25
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:34.125
yet remains entirely within it –

26
00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:35.375
in the same way,

27
00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:38.125
all living beings are free in this world

28
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:41.958
yet remain dependent on Lord Krishna.

29
00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.125
But have you

30
00:01:43.125 --> 00:01:44.083
ever seen the sky

31
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:47.291
being affected by the movement of the wind?

32
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:48.333
No.

33
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:51.083
In the same way, Lord Krishna
 remains unaffected

34
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:55.041
by the activities of all living beings.

35
00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:55.708
Just as

36
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:59.250
wind cannot exist without the sky,

37
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.375
creation cannot exist without Lord Krishna.

38
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:05.416
Through this analogy, we can understand 

39
00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:07.250
His extraordinary power –

40
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.750
He is the master of all creation,

41
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.583
everything is under Him,

42
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.291
yet He is not obstructed

43
00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:16.583
by any being, event, or thing.

44
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:19.791
It is also important for us to understand –

45
00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:21.458
just as the wind can move

46
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.708
in any direction within the sky,

47
00:02:23.708 --> 00:02:26.375
but cannot go beyond it –

48
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:28.250
in the same way,

49
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.708
every living being has

50
00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:31.000
some freedom,

51
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.291
but that freedom is limited –

52
00:02:33.291 --> 00:02:34.291
balanced and granted

53
00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:38.208
by Lord Krishna Himself.

54
00:02:38.208 --> 00:02:41.333
Like, The scriptures too describe

55
00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:44.958
that wind, the sun, and all natural elements

56
00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:48.041
function according to Lord Krishna’s command.

57
00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:49.916
He is the one who governs all of creation,

58
00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:51.958
yet remains free.

59
00:02:51.958 --> 00:02:54.041
We humans, on the other hand,

60
00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:56.291
get attached to the things

61
00:02:56.291 --> 00:02:59.500
we care for –

62
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.041
and this attachment becomes
 the cause of our suffering.

63
00:03:03.041 --> 00:03:05.791
It is the extraordinary glory of Lord Krishna

64
00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:09.125
that even as the master of all creation,

65
00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:12.250
 He gives us everything selflessly.

66
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.291
And this is what inspires us

67
00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:16.416
to be grateful to Him

68
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:19.958
and to remain absorbed in His devotion.

69
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.458
Tell Me –

70
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:31.000
a river flows with complete freedom.

71
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.416
But what would happen

72
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:36.291
if it broke its banks –

73
00:03:36.291 --> 00:03:37.958
its own boundaries?

74
00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:40.916
Destruction. Is that not so?

75
00:03:40.916 --> 00:03:42.416
In the same way,

76
00:03:42.416 --> 00:03:44.916
when you walk the path of dharma,

77
00:03:44.916 --> 00:03:47.500
you remain free –

78
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.666
yet within bounds.

79
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:52.166
Because freedom does not mean

80
00:03:52.166 --> 00:03:55.166
doing whatever comes to mind.

81
00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:58.250
Your freedom is like the wind –

82
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.625
free within the sky,

83
00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:04.333
yet always within its limits.

84
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:07.708
Just like the wind, your freedom too

85
00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:09.333
has its boundaries –

86
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:13.791
morality and responsibility.

87
00:04:13.791 --> 00:04:17.708
And these boundaries are essential.

88
00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:20.541
Because, Without them,

89
00:04:20.541 --> 00:04:22.791
your life will fill with chaos

90
00:04:22.791 --> 00:04:25.208
and discontent.

91
00:04:25.208 --> 00:04:27.291
The decisions you make

92
00:04:27.291 --> 00:04:29.750
matter greatly –

93
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.125
for you and for those around you.

94
00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:33.791
If they stay within the bounds

95
00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:36.166
of dharma and ethics,

96
00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:39.000
they bring balance and harmony.

97
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.375
But if they do not,

98
00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:44.208
they can become a cause of regret.

99
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:47.791
Always remember one thing,

100
00:04:47.791 --> 00:04:50.083
true freedom is that in which

101
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:53.791
your actions are purposeful,

102
00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:56.333
you can serve others,

103
00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:59.458
and you remain connected to truth.

104
00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:01.708
This is the state

105
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:05.708
where you will experience real freedom.

106
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.708
In family life,

107
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:14.750
it is very important to have a balance

108
00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.708
between freedom and its boundaries.

109
00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.166
Children always want

110
00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:22.333
complete freedom.

111
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:25.041
But imagine – if you gave the children at home

112
00:05:25.041 --> 00:05:28.916
total, unrestricted freedom – 
what would happen?

113
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:31.791
Without guiding values

114
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:35.125
or discipline, they could move in directions

115
00:05:35.125 --> 00:05:36.958
that may be harmful –

116
00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:40.875
for themselves or for others.

117
00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:44.458
But this does not mean you 
impose harsh and rigid rules on them –

118
00:05:44.458 --> 00:05:46.083
because that can hinder

119
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:49.958
their mental development and creativity.

120
00:05:49.958 --> 00:05:53.083
As parents or elders,

121
00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:54.333
set the boundaries

122
00:05:54.333 --> 00:05:57.458
of dharma and ethics.

123
00:05:57.458 --> 00:06:01.416
Teach every family member

124
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:05.250
values like respect and
 compassion toward one another.

125
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.875
Within these boundaries,

126
00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:09.500
give your loved ones the freedom

127
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.041
to make decisions and learn from experience.

128
00:06:13.041 --> 00:06:14.208
Along with that,

129
00:06:14.208 --> 00:06:17.666
guide them with principles

130
00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:20.625
that will make them steady in life.

131
00:06:20.625 --> 00:06:23.916
This balance will make them capable

132
00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.208
and strong in decision-making –

133
00:06:26.208 --> 00:06:29.000
not narrow their thinking.

134
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.666
Remember –

135
00:06:30.666 --> 00:06:32.000
when freedom exists

136
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.041
within healthy boundaries,

137
00:06:35.041 --> 00:06:38.125
relationships become warmer

138
00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:42.833
and your loved ones grow

139
00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:44.583
in a more harmonious way.

140
00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:52.000
As a leader of an organization,

141
00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.333
what should your duty be?

142
00:06:55.333 --> 00:06:56.500
What happened?

143
00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.333
Got worried listening to the question?

144
00:07:00.333 --> 00:07:01.916
Don’t worry –

145
00:07:01.916 --> 00:07:03.000
I am here,

146
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.333
let me explain.

147
00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:07.916
As a leader of an organization,

148
00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:10.833
your duty is to set the goals
 of your organisation clearly.

149
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:14.000
Because without a clear goal,

150
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.083
confusion can arise in the path to success.

151
00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:19.916
But this does not mean

152
00:07:20.375 --> 00:07:21.708
you control

153
00:07:21.708 --> 00:07:23.666
every small detail.

154
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:25.875
If you over-control

155
00:07:25.875 --> 00:07:28.166
every process,

156
00:07:28.166 --> 00:07:30.833
the creativity and imagination

157
00:07:30.833 --> 00:07:33.833
of your team members will not develop –

158
00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:37.500
and their interest in the work will fade.

159
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.375
Remember –

160
00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:41.583
it is the balance between freedom

161
00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:44.416
and structure that defines

162
00:07:44.416 --> 00:07:47.458
great leadership.

163
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:50.250
Establish a framework of ethical
 values, timelines,

164
00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.750
and priorities.

165
00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.375
Once these boundaries are set,

166
00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:59.625
trust your team

167
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:03.541
to find creative solutions

168
00:08:03.541 --> 00:08:05.541
and fresh perspectives within them.

169
00:08:05.541 --> 00:08:06.833
For example –

170
00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:10.791
if a task needs to be completed in a week,

171
00:08:10.791 --> 00:08:12.208
instead of controlling

172
00:08:12.208 --> 00:08:14.541
every small step,

173
00:08:14.541 --> 00:08:16.500
share the goal

174
00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.375
and let your team complete it

175
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:21.458
in their own way, using their own strengths.

176
00:08:21.458 --> 00:08:25.583
Stay in the role of a guide,

177
00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:27.541
not a controller.

178
00:08:27.541 --> 00:08:28.750
This approach

179
00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.333
will not only

180
00:08:29.333 --> 00:08:32.750
develop your team’s creativity,

181
00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:36.208
but also give them confidence.

182
00:08:36.208 --> 00:08:39.500
They will trust you fully.

183
00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.500
And that is what will make you successful.

184
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.208
Remember – when freedom exists within clear

185
00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:51.291
boundaries, growth is certain.
